  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating skewness based on whether a greater portion of probability is assigned to unfavorable outcomes. The individual did not refer to this concept or consider the relative mass of probability on unfavorable outcomes. Instead, their justification focuses on the higher probability of a positive outcome (34% vs. 33%) and the identical worst-case outcome. This reflects a focus on expected probability of winning rather than the shape of the distribution (skewness). The individual's reasoning is inconsistent with the skewness-based preference, which would favor Lottery B due to its higher weight on unfavorable outcomes. There is no indication in the verbal report that the individual considered or applied the concept of skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
